{"purpose":"Record a retirement-graph DEADLOCK: a requirement cannot be retired when its implementing decision is a superseded ADR, because the `supersedes` edge from the still-active successor blocks retiring the predecessor, and the predecessor's `derives-from` then blocks retiring the requirement.","content":"Concrete chain (EKA v2, M6/sto:team-collaboration-requirement-retire): `adr:solo-author-model` (existence active) --supersedes--\u003e `adr:029-assigned-work-membership` (existence active) --derives-from--\u003e `req:team-collaboration` (existence active). `eka retire` blocks a target when another ACTIVE published line references it via depends-on/derives-from/validates/supersedes/amends, and \"active\" is decided by EXISTENCE state (`eka-cli/cmd/retire.go:589`, `retireBlockerRels` L174-177). So: retire(req:team-collaboration) is refused (blocked by adr:029 derives-from); retire(adr:029) is refused (blocked by adr:solo-author-model supersedes). No legal retire order exists. `contentState: amended` does NOT help either, because the AGENTS.md constraint index only includes existenceState==active (`eka-core/contexts/constraints.go:43`). Workarounds are all lossy: `eka unrelate` rewrites provenance (and risks the revision state-reset foot-gun), or `--force` (bypasses the invariant).","investigationSummary":"Verified against the live store: `eka context` shows the derives-from/supersedes chain and states; read the retire blocker implementation (`cmd/retire.go` retireBlockerRels + the active check at L589) and the constraint index filter (`contexts/constraints.go:43`). Encountered while executing the team-collaboration requirement-retire WI.","conclusion":"Semantic gap in the retire graph: a `supersedes` edge from an ACTIVE successor should NOT block retiring the PREDECESSOR (the successor exists precisely to outlive it), or the superseded ADR should be retirable while its successor stays. Until fixed, retiring a requirement whose decision was superseded is impossible without a lossy workaround. Fix candidate for the expanded EKA v2 milestone."}